+### Record subtyping: `Cannot infer parameter 'A' … Candidate is: SomeRecord {R}` (2026-10-12)
+
+**Repro:** a path chain `p *> pmap F q *> r` proving an equality between two record values, e.g. two linear maps `LinearMap U U`.
+
+**Error:** `Cannot infer parameter 'A' of definition '*>' — Candidate is: LinearMap {R}`.
+
+**Why:** a record type with more fields implemented (`LinearMap U U`) is a subtype of one with fewer (`LinearMap {R}`), so the carrier type of the chain is not determined.
+
+**Fix:** prove the equality pointwise (`exts \lam v => …`), or give `*>` its type explicitly.
+
+**Diagnostic:** the "candidate" is the bare record name with almost none of its parameters.
+
+---
+
+### `\type` synonym not unfolded: `Cannot solve equation Rec … / E` (2026-10-12)
+
+**Repro:** `\type T => Rec A B`; a value `x : Rec A B` (e.g. built with `\cowith`) is passed where an element of a class instance with carrier `T` is expected.
+
+**Fix:** convert explicitly with an identity function of type `Rec A B -> T` (the library defines such functions, e.g. `Sym.fromEquiv`), or declare the value at type `T`.
+
+**Diagnostic:** one side is a concrete record type, the other the carrier field `E` of an instance whose carrier is a `\type` synonym of that record.
+
+---
