+**`-- |` is a single-line doc comment.** Continuation lines written as `--   more text` after a `-- |` line are ordinary comments and are *not* part of the documentation (the parser's `DOC_SINGLE_LINE_START` covers one line; the pretty-printer emits `{- | ... -}` whenever a description has more than one line). A doc comment that spans several lines must be a `{- | ... -}` block — and then the `{-`/`-}` audit above applies to its text (e.g. write `g^{ -1}`).
